# /etc/gitconfig -- the SYSTEM tier, read before ~/.gitconfig.
#
# This is exe.dev-specific, which is exactly why it lives in the image and not
# in the chezmoi dotfiles: those are cross-platform and must stay that way.
# Because git reads system -> global -> local, this composes with the
# chezmoi-managed ~/.gitconfig without touching it.
#
# The exe.dev GitHub integration exposes every accessible repo at
# https://github.int.exe.xyz/OWNER/REPO and picks the right integration itself,
# so one rewrite per owner makes `git clone https://github.com/...` just work
# with no token on the VM and no change to muscle memory.
#
# Scoped to the owner prefix on purpose. A blanket github.com rewrite would send
# public third-party clones through the integration too, and a repo with no
# matching integration FAILS rather than falling through to the public endpoint.
# git picks the longest matching insteadOf prefix, so these are exact.

[url "https://github.int.exe.xyz/andreweick/"]
	insteadOf = https://github.com/andreweick/
	insteadOf = git@github.com:andreweick/

[url "https://github.int.exe.xyz/missionfocus/"]
	insteadOf = https://github.com/missionfocus/
	insteadOf = git@github.com:missionfocus/
